</div><section id="shopify-section-template--18371451813971__rich_text_Y9Qa6H" class="shopify-section section"><link href="//naturaltein.in/cdn/shop/t/50/assets/section-rich-text.css?v=155362634389899593471764158812" rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" media="all" />
<div class="colgne-certification-list isolate">
  <div class="rich-text content-container color-scheme-1 gradient rich-text--full-width content-container--full-width section-template--18371451813971__rich_text_Y9Qa6H-padding">
    <div class="rich-text__wrapper rich-text__wrapper--left page-width">
      <div class="rich-text__blocks left"><h2
                class="rich-text__heading rte inline-richtext h1"
                
                
              >
                What is the Colognes List®? Does NATURALTEIN have whey protein certification?
              </h2><div
                class="rich-text__text rte"
                
                
              >
                <p>The Olympic Training Center Rhineland, Germany, started Cologne List®. OSP Director Michael Scharf believed this list would serve as a part of the center’s duty of care to athletes. The first list came in 2006, listing 25 products.</p><p>Cologne List® makes sure there is no problem of contamination in nutritional supplements.</p><p>All products on the Cologne List® have to pass the Center for Preventive Doping Research (CePreDo) test at the German Sport University in Cologne. Of course, not all products stand up to standards. Those products that successfully pass a label check at the Center for Preventive Doping Research (CePreDo) go on for further testing and analysis.</p><p>Selected products go through testing for anabolic-androgenic steroids and stimulants. Once the testing and analysis are complete, Cologne List publishes the tested products (which do not contain unlawful or harmful ingredients). One can consume these products safely as they are free from banned substances.</p><p>Since 2017, the Cologne List has been the world’s biggest doping prevention platform for nutritional protein supplements. It has reduced unintentional doping incidents and health risks in those who consume harmful supplements.</p><p></p>
              </div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>


</section><section id="shopify-section-template--18371451813971__rich_text_txCTDM" class="shopify-section section"><link href="//naturaltein.in/cdn/shop/t/50/assets/section-rich-text.css?v=155362634389899593471764158812" rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" media="all" />
<div class="cologne-list-mean-sec isolate">
  <div class="rich-text content-container color-scheme-1 gradient rich-text--full-width content-container--full-width section-template--18371451813971__rich_text_txCTDM-padding">
    <div class="rich-text__wrapper rich-text__wrapper--left page-width">
      <div class="rich-text__blocks left"><h2
                class="rich-text__heading rte inline-richtext h1"
                
                
              >
                What does it mean to have the Cologne List® certified logo?
              </h2><div
                class="rich-text__text rte"
                
                
              >
                <p>NATURALTEIN is India’s first and only brand with Cologne whey protein certification.</p><p>Our whey protein has been tested for doping substances. You won’t find stimulants such as DMAA, OMBA, phenylethylamine (e.g., BMPEA), and hyper caffeination in NATURALTEIN protein.</p><p>Many athletes prefer our whey protein because it eliminates doping risks and is safe for consumption.</p>
              </div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>


</section><section id="shopify-section-template--18371451813971__rich_text_i8MQna" class="shopify-section section"><link href="//naturaltein.in/cdn/shop/t/50/assets/section-rich-text.css?v=155362634389899593471764158812" rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" media="all" />
<div class="colgne-protien-powder isolate">
  <div class="rich-text content-container color-scheme-1 gradient rich-text--full-width content-container--full-width section-template--18371451813971__rich_text_i8MQna-padding">
    <div class="rich-text__wrapper rich-text__wrapper--left page-width">
      <div class="rich-text__blocks left"><h2
                class="rich-text__heading rte inline-richtext h1"
                
                
              >
                Why buy certified protein powder?
              </h2><div
                class="rich-text__text rte"
                
                
              >
                <p>One of the reasons people choose to<a href="/pages/whey-protein-isolate" title="Whey Protein Isolate"> buy certified protein powder</a> is because it has enough protein than consuming different whole foods. Protein powders are also convenient for getting your body’s nutrients without preparing and cooking meals.</p><p>Another reason to buy certified protein powder is that it is often fortified with other nutrients, such as vitamins and minerals. This makes a great option for people who may not be able to get all the nutrients they need from their diet. Protein powders can also help people meet their daily protein needs when trying to lose weight or build muscle.</p><p>Certified protein powder is also a good choice for people who have food allergies or intolerances.</p><p>For example,<a href="/products/natural-whey-protein-concentrate-vanilla-naturally-flavoured-gmo-free-gluten-free-23-1g-protein" title="Natural Whey Protein Concentrate – Vanilla (Naturally Flavoured, GMO Free, Gluten Free, 23.1g Protein)"> NATURALTEIN protein powders</a> consist of natural ingredients and are free of artificial sweeteners, flavors, etc. Thus, our protein is a safe option for people with food allergies or sensitivities.</p>
              </div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>


</section><div id="shopify-section-template--18371451813971__advantages_of_certified_grass_section_rFWBcq" class="shopify-section cologne-certified-advantages-section"><div class="cologne-certified-advantages-section ">
  <div class="container">
    
    <div class="cologne-certified-wrapper">
      
      
      
        <div class="certified-title-block">
          <h2 class="certified-title">Advantages of certified grass fed whey protein supplement</h2>
        </div>
      
  
      
      
        <div class="certified-content-block">
          <p class="certified-content"><p>If you are looking to improve your overall health and fitness, you may consider adding a<a href="/pages/whey-protein-concentrate" title="Whey Protein Concentrate"> certified whey protein supplement</a> to your diet. Whey protein is one of the most beneficial types of protein available, offering a wide range of health benefits.</p><p>Make sure you buy the ones with whey protein certification. Only these supplements can help you build muscle, lose weight, and improve overall health. Here are some of the top benefits of whey protein:</p></p>
        </div>
      
  
      
      
        <div class="certified-blocks-wrapper">
          
            
              <div class="certified-block">
                <h3 class="certified-block-title"><strong>1.</strong> Whey protein is a great source of protein.</h3>
                <div class="certified-block-description"><p>Protein ensures muscle building, and whey protein is one of the best protein sources available. A single scoop of whey protein has about 20-25 grams of protein, more than enough to support muscle growth.</p></div>
              </div>
            
          
            
              <div class="certified-block">
                <h3 class="certified-block-title">2. Whey protein supplement is easily digestible</h3>
                <div class="certified-block-description"><p>NATURALTEIN protein is very easy for the body to digest, making it an ideal choice for post-workout recovery. When you consume whey protein, your body can quickly absorb the nutrients and start rebuilding muscle tissue.</p></div>
              </div>
            
          
            
              <div class="certified-block">
                <h3 class="certified-block-title">3. Whey protein can help you lose weight.</h3>
                <div class="certified-block-description"><p>If you are trying to lose weight, whey protein can be a helpful addition to your diet. Whey protein helps promote satiety, which means you will feel fuller for longer after eating. This can help to reduce your overall calorie intake and promote weight loss.</p></div>
              </div>
            
          
            
              <div class="certified-block">
                <h3 class="certified-block-title">4. NATURALTEIN protein is high in essential amino acids</h3>
                <div class="certified-block-description"><p>Amino acids are the building blocks of protein. Whey protein is high in amino acids such as leucine, isoleucine, and valine. These amino acids are vital for triggering muscle growth and recovery.</p></div>
              </div>
            
          
            
              <div class="certified-block">
                <h3 class="certified-block-title">5. Whey protein supplements can boost your immune system.</h3>
                <div class="certified-block-description"><p>Whey protein is rich in immunoglobulins, antibodies that help fight off infection. Consuming whey protein can help to boost your immune system and keep you healthy.</p></div>
              </div>
            
          
            
              <div class="certified-block">
                <h3 class="certified-block-title">6. Whey protein is high in calcium</h3>
                <div class="certified-block-description"><p>Calcium is important for bone health, and whey protein is a great mineral source. A single scoop (33 gram) of whey protein powder isolate contains about 160 mg of calcium, enough to meet your daily needs.</p></div>
              </div>
            
          
            
              <div class="certified-block">
                <h3 class="certified-block-title">7. Whey protein can help you manage stress</h3>
                <div class="certified-block-description"><p>Whey protein contains high levels of the amino acid tryptophan (6%), a precursor to serotonin. Serotonin is a neurotransmitter that helps to regulate mood and can help to reduce stress levels. Based on one study, stress-vulnerable subjects who took whey protein experienced enhanced brain cognition and reduced anxiety.</p></div>
              </div>
            
          
            
              <div class="certified-block">
                <h3 class="certified-block-title">8. Whey protein is rich in antioxidants</h3>
                <div class="certified-block-description"><p>Whey protein is rich in antioxidants, molecules that help to protect cells from damage. These antioxidants can help to reduce the risk of some chronic diseases, such as heart disease and cancer.</p></div>
              </div>
            
          
            
              <div class="certified-block">
                <h3 class="certified-block-title">9. Whey protein supplement is low in lactose</h3>
                <div class="certified-block-description"><p>Lactose is a type of sugar found in milk, and it can be difficult for some people to digest. However, whey protein is very low in lactose, making it a good choice for those who are lactose intolerant.</p></div>
              </div>
            
          
            
              <div class="certified-block">
                <h3 class="certified-block-title">10. Whey protein is a complete protein</h3>
                <div class="certified-block-description"><p>Whey protein is a complete protein, meaning it contains essential amino acids that your body needs to build muscle and lose weight. Certified whey protein supplements can offer a wide range of health benefits, making them a great addition to your diet.</p><p>Make NATURALTEIN your go-to brand to enjoy health benefits like many people have been doing. Get on with your fitness journey; waste no more time!</p></div>
              </div>
            
          
        </div>
      
    
    </div>
  </div>
</div>


